 "done_when": "The customer is verified and logged, eligibility is confirmed, and the customer has agreed to the account with the lowest ATM fees among those that meet their early direct deposit need, age and hard needs. For a 2-day need at out-of-network ATMs abroad, the Bluest Account has the lowest per-withdrawal Rho-Bank fee: $2.00 vs Purple $2.50 vs Evergreen 1% capped at $2.50 plus 2% min $3.00. Bluest is excluded when the customer cannot deposit $75,000. For no foreign transaction fees plus a multi-currency wallet on a few-thousand-dollar balance, the account is the Purple Account. A customer may give a monthly withdrawal count, amount and duration with no early direct deposit or other hard need. In that case the totals were computed in compute_totals, and the account with the lowest total was recommended with its total and its other fees: at out-of-network ATMs abroad that is the Green Fee-Free Account, with $0.00 foreign and $0.00 out-of-network Rho-Bank fees. If the customer already accepted a checking class earlier (e.g. from the savings + card combination), that class was confirmed and opened. open_bank_account_4821 has returned a new account (and any fee waiver has been explained), or the customer has been told why it could not be opened. If the customer also asked to close an old checking account, closing_personal_checking_accounts follows."
}

